{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-73e1b731-1ff3-4185-9e91-75393f365d12","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa3cf47af941d194","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-imnpjyjx/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E005.md","content":"# Split-server artifact serving topology in the MLflow operator\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic implements the split-server topology in the MLflow operator: when split-server artifact serving is enabled via an opt-in in the MLflow CR spec, the operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, propagates the workspace configuration to it using the same mechanisms as the main tracking deployment, and configures the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to that dedicated instance. This is a split-server topology, not a single-deployment configuration toggle (Staff Engineer input). The routing mechanism follows the outcome of the artifact traffic routing investigation. Per the Staff Engineer input, no `spec.artifactsOnly.workspaceAware` CR field or new server flag is introduced — the dedicated instance runs with the existing combined flags.\n\n## Scope\n\n- New Helm chart templates (following the operator's Helm-in-operator pattern: CR spec converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, applied via Server-Side Apply) for the artifacts-only Deployment, its Service, and its HTTPRoute.\n- An opt-in in the MLflow CR spec that enables the split-server topology; users configure a single MLflow CR rather than managing individual resources.\n- Propagation of the workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`, `--serve-artifacts`, `--artifacts-only`) to the dedicated instance using the same configuration mechanisms used for the main tracking deployment.\n- The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment (authentication layer unchanged).\n- Configuration of artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated instance, per the mechanism selected by the routing investigation (gateway-level path routing, or wiring tracking-server delegation configuration if that outcome is selected).\n- HTTPRoute resources created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n- Operator validation that rejects MLflow CR configurations where the artifacts-only instance lacks the workspace flags, so misconfiguration cannot silently bypass workspace validation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, reconciliation creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment (distinct Deployment resources present with the correct flag combinations).\n- The artifacts-only Deployment's container command runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts` (verifiable in the rendered Deployment spec).\n- Artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment is routed to the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the selected routing mechanism, and artifact requests through the main deployment's route are served by the dedicated instance.\n- The operator rejects MLflow CR configurations that enable the split topology without the workspace flags on the artifacts-only instance (validation error, no deployment that would bypass workspace validation).\n- HTTPRoute creation remains conditional on runtime Gateway API CRD discovery; reconciliation succeeds on clusters without the Gateway API CRDs (consistent with the existing optional-dependency pattern).\n- MLflow CRs that do not enable split-server artifact serving reconcile identically to current behavior (no new resources created; backwards compatible).\n- No new server flag and no `spec.artifactsOnly.workspaceAware` CR field is introduced; the dedicated instance is configured solely through the existing flags.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P1 HLR: \"MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute\" — primary coverage.\n- P1 HLR: \"Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\" — primary coverage (mechanism per the routing investigation outcome; if server-side delegation is selected, the server-side change is planned in the corresponding conditional branch).\n- Supports the P0 fail-closed/isolation HLRs operationally (operator validation prevents misconfigured deployments that would bypass workspace validation).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":63599,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-beddc54cf64e5d56","agent_id":"a5fc108e902f0ec98","session_id":"29d6ac74-9e14-4313-a4f4-972162f9d527","uuid":"c2679b8d-a88f-4c1c-9ab3-e99aa86e9ef4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:44:19.018Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009 into epics"}
