equests are denied with HTTP 503 indicating workspace validation is unavailable.\n  - Split topology: operator reconciliation creates the dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute with the correct flag combination, distinct from the main tracking Deployment.\n  - Split-server routing: artifact requests through the main deployment's route are served by the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n- Single-tenant deployment regression scenarios (workspace flags absent, current behavior preserved).\n- Non-artifact API surface checks in artifacts-only mode (tracking/registry endpoints remain disabled).\n- Documented results covering the multi-tenant, backwards-compatibility, single-tenant regression, fail-closed, and split-server routing scenarios.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The end-to-end suite executes all listed scenarios against the operator-deployed split-server topology and each scenario passes: member allow (HTTP 200, correct content), cross-workspace deny (HTTP 403 with insufficient-permissions message), no-workspace-flags backwards compatibility (HTTP 200 without workspace validation), workspace store unreachable (HTTP 503, fail-closed), distinct split-topology resources with the correct container flags, and artifact traffic routed through the main deployment served by the dedicated instance.\n- Single-tenant regression scenarios pass with workspace flags absent (current behavior preserved, no new resources beyond current operator behavior).\n- Non-artifact API endpoints remain disabled in artifacts-only mode across the tested topologies.\n- Validation results are documented, including the multi-tenant, backwards-compatibility, single-tenant regression, fail-closed, and split-server routing scenario outcomes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Verifies end-to-end the P0 HLRs: workspace-membership validation with HTTP 403 denials; fail-closed behavior when the workspace store is unreachable; single-tenant / no-workspace-flags backwards compatibility; combined-flag workspace-validated artifact serving.\n- Verifies end-to-end the P1 HLRs: operator-deployed dedicated artifacts-only Deployment/Service/HTTPRoute; main tracking deployment routing artifact traffic to the dedicated instance.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":64588,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-beddc54cf64e5d56","agent_id":"a5fc108e902f0ec98","session_id":"29d6ac74-9e14-4313-a4f4-972162f9d527","uuid":"40d7d841-0567-48b2-82a8-ee9ae09e4812","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:44:29.680Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009 into epics"}
