{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8c023977dac74ed","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n3\ttitle: Independent workspace resolution path in the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth\n4\t  plugin\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: if the investigation finds workspace resolution coupled to full\n16\t    tracking server initialization, the refactor scope it defines is added; if uncoupled,\n17\t    this epic reduces to verification with regression coverage\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Independent workspace resolution path in the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic verifies and, where needed, extends the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin so that workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only MLflow server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. It proceeds from the findings of the workspace-resolution initialization dependency investigation: if the plugin's workspace resolution is coupled to full tracking server initialization, the coupling is factored into an independent initialization path within the plugin; if uncoupled, this epic reduces to verification with regression coverage. Per the Staff Engineer input, workspace authorization reuses the existing auth plugin infrastructure — this epic must not prescribe new Kubernetes API mechanics (e.g., SelfSubjectAccessReview details), and the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup remain unchanged.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Verify the plugin's experiment-to-workspace resolution works when invoked from an artifacts-only server context with tracking and model registry stores uninitialized.\n44\t- If the investigation found coupling to the full server initialization path: refactor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, preserving behavior for the full tracking server path.\n45\t- Ensure experiment-to-workspace resolution succeeds for artifact request paths following the standard `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` layout (initial scope: S3 artifact store, the standard RHOAI configuration).\n46\t- Keep the existing registration and loading mechanisms (`mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group, `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) and the existing authorization model unchanged.\n47\t- Regression coverage for the tracking server's existing (non-artifact) workspace resolution.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Workspace resolution in the plugin returns the correct workspace assignment for artifact request paths with experiment-scoped layout, in a server context where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized (demonstrated by tests).\n52\t- If refactoring was required: workspace resolution initializes via an independent path that does not require tracking store or model registry store initialization, and the full tracking server's workspace resolution behavior is unchanged (regression tests pass).\n53\t- No changes are required to the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar setup or the `--app-name kubernetes-auth` authentication layer.\n54\t- The plugin introduces no new configuration surface beyond what the artifacts-only context requires, and no new Kubernetes API mechanics are prescribed beyond the existing auth plugin infrastructure.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- P1 HLR: \"Auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization\" — primary coverage.\n59\t- Enables (transitively) the P0 HLRs \"Artifact requests through the workspace-aware artifacts-only server are validated against workspace membership; requests from users without workspace membership are denied with HTTP 403\" and \"`--artifacts-only` can be combined with `--enable-workspaces` and `--workspace-store-uri`\".\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaca424bb73b2f18","agent_id":"adb1d7279032b26ad","session_id":"29d6ac74-9e14-4313-a4f4-972162f9d527","uuid":"be25901d-5a9d-440f-b2c4-b98e36f75c50","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:46:52.433Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8c023977dac74ed","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
