{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93b71c10095c6e76","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n3\ttitle: Workspace-aware artifacts-only serving in the MLflow tracking server\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: -1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 5\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Workspace-aware artifacts-only serving in the MLflow tracking server\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic makes the MLflow tracking server's `--artifacts-only` mode composable with the existing `--enable-workspaces` flag, producing workspace-validated, fail-closed artifact serving. No new server flag is introduced (Staff Engineer input): the workspace-aware behavior emerges from combining existing flags. When both flags are set, the server requires an explicit `--workspace-store-uri`, initializes only the workspace provider needed to validate artifact requests, and leaves tracking stores, model registry stores, and non-artifact API endpoints uninitialized/disabled. Workspace authorization delegates to the existing auth plugin infrastructure, whose workspace resolution capability in the artifacts-only context is delivered by the plugin work this epic builds against.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Server startup: allow `--artifacts-only` together with `--enable-workspaces`; require an explicit `--workspace-store-uri` when both are set (fail to start with a clear error if missing); initialize only the workspace provider.\n39\t- Artifact request handling: resolve each artifact request's path to its parent experiment (artifacts stored under experiment-scoped paths, e.g., `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`), look up the experiment's workspace assignment via the workspace store, and delegate authorization to the existing auth plugin infrastructure. Requests failing workspace validation receive HTTP 403 with an error indicating insufficient workspace permissions.\n40\t- Fail-closed behavior: when workspace-aware mode is active but the workspace store is unreachable, artifact requests are denied (HTTP 503 indicating workspace validation is unavailable) rather than served without validation.\n41\t- Backwards compatibility: `--artifacts-only` without `--enable-workspaces` retains current behavior; omitting either flag preserves current behavior; no existing API contracts, CLI arguments, or configuration keys change meaning.\n42\t- Audit logging (P2, bundled): workspace access denials in artifact serving are logged through server logs, on the same denial path the validation creates.\n43\t- Performance contingency (per the strategy's risk mitigation): measure per-request overhead of workspace validation and implement short-TTL caching of workspace membership decisions consistent with the tracking server's existing auth-path caching patterns if measurement shows need.\n44\t- Initial artifact-path resolution scope: S3 artifact store (standard RHOAI configuration); limitations for non-standard artifact roots documented.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- Given the server started with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes://`, a user who is a member of workspace A requesting an artifact belonging to an experiment in workspace A receives HTTP 200 with the correct artifact content.\n49\t- Given the same deployment, a user who is a member of workspace A but not workspace B requesting an artifact belonging to an experiment in workspace B receives HTTP 403 with an error message indicating insufficient workspace permissions.\n50\t- Given `--artifacts-only` set without `--enable-workspaces`, any authenticated user's artifact request is served without workspace validation (HTTP 200 regardless of workspace membership) — current behavior preserved.\n51\t- Given workspace-aware serving active and the workspace store (Kubernetes API) unreachable, artifact requests are denied with HTTP 503 indicating workspace validation is unavailable (fail-closed).\n52\t- The server started with both flags but without an explicit `--workspace-store-uri` fails to start with a clear error message.\n53\t- In workspace-aware artifacts-only mode, tracking stores and model registry stores remain uninitialized and non-artifact API endpoints remain disabled.\n54\t- No new server flag is introduced, and no existing CLI argument or configuration key changes meaning.\n55\t- Workspace access denials in artifact serving are recorded in server logs.\n56\t- Per-request workspace validation overhead is measured and documented; short-TTL caching of workspace membership decisions is implemented if the measurement shows need, consistent with existing auth-path caching patterns.\n57\t- Artifact path resolution supports the S3 artifact store's experiment-scoped layout; limitations for non-standard artifact roots are documented.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- P0 HLR: \"`--artifacts-only` can be combined with `--enable-workspaces` and `--workspace-store-uri` to enable workspace-validated artifact serving\" — primary coverage.\n62\t- P0 HLR: \"Artifact requests through the workspace-aware artifacts-only server are validated against workspace membership; requests from users without workspace membership are denied with HTTP 403\" — primary coverage.\n63\t- P0 HLR: \"Workspace-aware artifact serving is fail-closed: if the workspace store is unreachable, requests are denied\" — primary coverage.\n64\t- P0 HLR: \"Single-tenant deployments and configurations without `--enable-workspaces` retain current behavior with no changes\" — primary coverage.\n65\t- P2 HLR: \"Audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving through server logs\" — bundled (same denial call sites and request-handling surface as the P0 validation work; not separately schedulable — a split would force a second pass over the identical code path).\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaca424bb73b2f18","agent_id":"adb1d7279032b26ad","session_id":"29d6ac74-9e14-4313-a4f4-972162f9d527","uuid":"f21f2ad8-bb3f-4d0e-9254-76f04f01b1bf","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:46:55.154Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-93b71c10095c6e76","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
