{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1ac92f626b25f61","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n3\ttitle: Artifact traffic routing mechanism for the split-server MLflow topology\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Artifact traffic routing mechanism for the split-server MLflow topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis Investigation determines how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology, and whether the MLflow tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations. The strategy flags this as an open question owned by the MLflow Team that affects the HTTPRoute design and the operator implementation's approach. There are two bounded outcomes: (A) gateway-level path-based routing via HTTPRoute with no tracking server change, or (B) tracking-server-side configuration that delegates artifact operations to the dedicated instance. The outcome selects a conditional decomposition branch for the server-side work.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Analyze the operator's existing routing implementation (Gateway API HTTPRoute handling with runtime CRD discovery) and the tracking server's artifact-serving/proxy behavior to determine which routing mechanism is viable and appropriate.\n34\t- Decide between outcome A (HTTPRoute path-based routing from the main deployment's route to the dedicated instance; no server change) and outcome B (tracking server configuration change to delegate artifact operations).\n35\t- Define the HTTPRoute design implications for the artifacts-only instance under the selected outcome, consistent with the operator's conditional CRD discovery pattern for optional dependencies.\n36\t- Identify the configuration impacts on the main tracking deployment under the selected outcome.\n37\t- Deliverable: a design note recording the selected mechanism, the verdict on whether server-side delegation is required, and the routing design implications.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- The design note records the selected routing mechanism (gateway-level path routing vs tracking-server delegation) with selection rationale grounded in the operator's existing routing implementation and the server's artifact-serving behavior.\n42\t- The design note states explicitly, as a pass/fail verdict, whether the MLflow tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations.\n43\t- The HTTPRoute design implications for the artifacts-only instance are defined, consistent with the operator's conditional CRD discovery pattern for Gateway API resources.\n44\t- The configuration impacts on the main tracking deployment are identified, leaving no residual unknowns that would change the operator implementation's approach.\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- Covers the strategy open question \"How should the operator configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking server to the dedicated artifacts-only instance?\" and informs (gates) the P1 HLRs \"MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute\" and \"Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\".\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaca424bb73b2f18","agent_id":"adb1d7279032b26ad","session_id":"29d6ac74-9e14-4313-a4f4-972162f9d527","uuid":"9768905a-586e-4d20-9f52-47f753927b6e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:46:55.752Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1ac92f626b25f61","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
