{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f46debe43e6fdae","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E006\n3\ttitle: End-to-end integration testing of workspace-aware artifact serving\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 4\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# End-to-end integration testing of workspace-aware artifact serving\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic delivers the end-to-end integration validation of workspace-aware artifact serving across the full split-server topology: the workspace-aware artifacts-only MLflow server, the extended auth plugin workspace resolution, and the operator-deployed dedicated instance with artifact traffic routing. The strategy's effort estimate calls out integration testing as a distinct work stream (multi-tenant workspace scenarios, backwards compatibility, single-tenant regression, fail-closed edge cases, split-server routing), and its proposed acceptance criteria are end-to-end Given/When/Then scenarios that require the complete topology. This epic spans all three strategy components (MLflow server, MLflow operator, mlflow-kubernetes-plugins); the MLflow component is the most relevant surface since the capability under test is MLflow artifact serving behavior.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- An end-to-end scenario suite running against the operator-deployed split-server topology, covering the strategy's proposed acceptance criteria:\n40\t  - Multi-tenant allow: a workspace member requesting an artifact of an experiment in their workspace receives HTTP 200 with correct content.\n41\t  - Multi-tenant deny: a user member of workspace A but not workspace B requesting workspace B's artifact receives HTTP 403 with an insufficient-permissions error.\n42\t  - Backwards compatibility: artifacts-only serving without workspace flags serves artifacts without workspace validation (current behavior).\n43\t  - Fail-closed: with the workspace store unreachable, artifact requests are denied with HTTP 503 indicating workspace validation is unavailable.\n44\t  - Split topology: operator reconciliation creates the dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute with the correct flag combination, distinct from the main tracking Deployment.\n45\t  - Split-server routing: artifact requests through the main deployment's route are served by the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n46\t- Single-tenant deployment regression scenarios (workspace flags absent, current behavior preserved).\n47\t- Non-artifact API surface checks in artifacts-only mode (tracking/registry endpoints remain disabled).\n48\t- Documented results covering the multi-tenant, backwards-compatibility, single-tenant regression, fail-closed, and split-server routing scenarios.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- The end-to-end suite executes all listed scenarios against the operator-deployed split-server topology and each scenario passes: member allow (HTTP 200, correct content), cross-workspace deny (HTTP 403 with insufficient-permissions message), no-workspace-flags backwards compatibility (HTTP 200 without workspace validation), workspace store unreachable (HTTP 503, fail-closed), distinct split-topology resources with the correct container flags, and artifact traffic routed through the main deployment served by the dedicated instance.\n53\t- Single-tenant regression scenarios pass with workspace flags absent (current behavior preserved, no new resources beyond current operator behavior).\n54\t- Non-artifact API endpoints remain disabled in artifacts-only mode across the tested topologies.\n55\t- Validation results are documented, including the multi-tenant, backwards-compatibility, single-tenant regression, fail-closed, and split-server routing scenario outcomes.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- Verifies end-to-end the P0 HLRs: workspace-membership validation with HTTP 403 denials; fail-closed behavior when the workspace store is unreachable; single-tenant / no-workspace-flags backwards compatibility; combined-flag workspace-validated artifact serving.\n60\t- Verifies end-to-end the P1 HLRs: operator-deployed dedicated artifacts-only Deployment/Service/HTTPRoute; main tracking deployment routing artifact traffic to the dedicated instance.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaca424bb73b2f18","agent_id":"adb1d7279032b26ad","session_id":"29d6ac74-9e14-4313-a4f4-972162f9d527","uuid":"30d7f7d5-bffa-4e77-b918-a82fe94d4e3e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:46:59.175Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f46debe43e6fdae","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
