ured, the main tracking server delegates artifact operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance instead of serving/proxying them itself.\n43\t- Configuration surface limited to what the operator can set through its existing configuration mechanisms for the main tracking deployment; the exact keys/forms are an implementation decision for the team.\n44\t- No changes to workspace validation behavior for non-artifact operations, and no changes to the artifacts-only server's own behavior.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- Given a main tracking deployment configured for artifact-operations delegation, artifact requests to the main tracking server are served via the dedicated artifacts-only instance (requests reach the dedicated instance and responses return through the main deployment).\n49\t- Without delegation configured, the main tracking server retains its current artifact-serving behavior (backwards compatible; no existing configuration key changes meaning).\n50\t- The delegation configuration is documentable and settable through the operator's existing configuration mechanisms for the main tracking deployment.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- P1 HLR: \"Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\" — conditional coverage under routing outcome B (the operator-side wiring of this configuration is carried by the operator split-topology epic in the main plan).\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaca424bb73b2f18","agent_id":"adb1d7279032b26ad","session_id":"29d6ac74-9e14-4313-a4f4-972162f9d527","uuid":"1d262730-d62b-4ca8-adb2-eda5304c1a67","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:47:04.075Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-93f44d2885143813","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
